  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Security Print",
    "overview": "Ledgerline is printed, not rendered. Every surface is a piece of security stationery: a mint security-tint ground under fine generated guilloche line-work, deep intaglio green that owns whole bands of the page, and paper documents (remittance advice, statement, cheque, application slip) laid on those bands with perforated stub edges and MICR-style code lines. The product is shown as the document it produces, never as a dashboard screenshot.\n\nDensity is that of a financial document: rows on fixed columns, hairline rules, tabular figures, written-out amounts. Colour is ink discipline. Green is the ink, plum is overprinted only where something needs a person, vermilion is overprinted only on things you can press. Display type is engraved Bodoni at large optical sizes; the working text is a plain grotesk; every figure and code sits in a monospace with tabular numerals.\n\nMotion is a single authored moment (the hero clearing pass) plus quiet state transitions; content is always visible by default and reduced motion shows the finished state.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Alternating bands: intaglio-green fields and mint-tint fields, with paper documents lifted onto them.",
      "Procedurally generated guilloche (wave bands, rose fields, hypotrochoid rosettes) behind every paper and band, each from its own seed.",
      "Rows on fixed columns; state restyles a row, never the grid.",
      "Three-ink colour logic: green structure, plum exceptions, vermilion actions.",
      "Bodoni display, Schibsted Grotesk text, Spline Sans Mono figures.",
      "Near-square corners (2-3px); perforation (2px dashed) is the divider between a document and its stub."
    ],
